{"id": "tea:jnanasara:1", "source": "src:jnanasara", "location": {"ref": "1", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "Seen by one full of being, consciousness and bliss, the world appears full; to one absorbed in borrowed splendour, it is only play.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate", "consciousness-mind"], "terms": ["trm:cidananda"], "teachers": ["tch:yasovijaya"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "notes": "First aṣṭaka (pūrṇatā); wording recalled in substance.", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:jnanasara:16.2", "source": "src:jnanasara", "location": {"ref": "16.2", "chapter": "16", "verse": "2", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "The calf of the impartial one's mind runs after the cow of reason; the monkey-mind of the petty dogmatist drags reason by the tail.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "dispute"], "terms": ["trm:madhyasthya"], "obstacles": ["obs:ekanta-view"], "teachers": ["tch:yasovijaya"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "notes": "Aṣṭaka on impartiality (mādhyasthya). Verse number recalled, not checked; the content is the unit author's recollection (skeleton).", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:jnanasara:32", "source": "src:jnanasara", "location": {"ref": "32", "section": null}, "paraphrase": "The knower takes refuge in all standpoints: attached to none, he gives each its place, and with impartial mind attains the highest bliss.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate", "consciousness-mind"], "concepts": ["cpt:nayavada", "cpt:anekantavada"], "teachers": ["tch:yasovijaya"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U35-jain-philosophy"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "notes": "Last aṣṭaka (sarvanayāśraya); recalled in substance.", "coverage": ["B2"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U35-jain-philosophy"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
